# angelOS: the charge of wireless mice, read from their dongles (the bar's ampoules,
# scripts/peripherals.py). Installed by extras/hid-access/install.sh; do not edit, an update
# writes it again.
#
# What it opens, and to whom:
#   - only the makers angelOS can ask (the list below is peripherals.py's);
#   - of their devices only the maker's configuration interface, and only when the helper
#     finds no input or output report in it: the dongle's keyboard and mouse interfaces stay
#     root's alone, so no program can read keys or movement through this rule;
#   - only to the user sitting at this computer (uaccess: logind's ACL, taken away at logout
#     or a switch to another seat) — never MODE="0666", never a group.
# The number must stay below 73: 73-seat-late.rules is what turns the tag into the ACL.

# LAMZU (the Aurora feature report)
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="373e", PROGRAM=="/usr/local/libexec/angelos-hid-feature-only %S%p", TAG+="uaccess"
